From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:35:30 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro: Add the VGPIO2AP sysreg

The system registers that latch the main PMIC's in-band interrupt (GIC
SPI 74 on this SoC), the way gs201.dtsi describes gs201's at 0x182f0000.
The PMIC node points at it with google,vgpio2ap-sysreg.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
index 3d3126ab9..4a1ea78aa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro.dtsi
@@ -1548,6 +1548,12 @@ cmu_apm: clock-controller@15400000 {
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
+		/* Latches the S2MPG14 PMIC's in-band interrupt (GIC SPI 74). */
+		sysreg_vgpio2ap: syscon@15090000 {
+			compatible = "google,zumapro-vgpio2ap-sysreg", "syscon";
+			reg = <0x0 0x15090000 0x1000>;
+		};
+
 		sysreg_apm: syscon@154204e0 {
 			compatible = "google,zumapro-apm-sysreg", "syscon";
 			/* Only the USI mode selectors. */
